    <string name="about_back">Back</string>
    <string name="about_tagline">On-device speech-to-text. Your audio never leaves your phone.</string>
    <string name="about_tagline_remote">Speech-to-text through a server you control. Your audio is uploaded to it.</string>
    <string name="about_two_ways">Two ways to use Scrib</string>
    <string name="about_own_h">Transcribe your own audio</string>
    <string name="about_own_b">Record straight into the app, or pick any audio file on your phone, and get the text — right here, fully offline.</string>
    <string name="about_own_b_remote">Record straight into the app, or pick any audio file on your phone, and get the text. The audio goes to your endpoint, is transcribed there, and the text comes back.</string>
    <string name="about_engine_h">A transcription engine for other apps</string>
    <string name="about_engine_b">Scrib also works in the background. Apps that support it — like Forkgram — can turn a voice message into text using Scrib, on your device. In that app\'s settings, choose Scrib as the offline transcriber. Nothing is uploaded.</string>
    <string name="about_engine_b_remote">Scrib also works in the background. Apps that support it — like Forkgram — can turn a voice message into text using Scrib. In that app\'s settings, choose Scrib as the transcriber. The recording is uploaded to your endpoint.</string>
    <string name="about_keyboard_h">Dictate into any app</string>
    <string name="about_keyboard_b">Scrib can act as a voice keyboard. Switch it on in your phone\'s keyboard settings, then press the microphone key of a keyboard like HeliBoard, or pick Scrib Voice from the keyboard switcher, and speak — the text goes straight into whatever you were writing, and your keyboard comes back when you stop.</string>
    <string name="about_models_h">Models</string>
    <string name="about_endpoint_h">Endpoint</string>
    <string name="about_models_b">Scrib transcribes with open speech models through one small ggml runtime: Whisper, Parakeet, SenseVoice, Canary, Moonshine, GigaAM and more. Download one on the main screen, or pick your language and Scrib fetches a fitting one. Bigger models are more accurate; keep several and switch anytime.</string>
    <string name="about_endpoint_b">There is no model on this phone and no inference code: Scrib Remote is the recorder, the uploader and the editor. Point it at any OpenAI-compatible server — whisper.cpp, faster-whisper, Speaches, LM Studio — or at Cloudflare Workers AI, and it sends the audio there over HTTPS, naming the address on screen.</string>
    <string name="about_dev_h">For developers</string>
    <string name="about_dev_b">Any app can use Scrib as an offline transcriber through the open Open Transcribe contract (org.opentranscribe.api) — a small AIDL service, no SDK and no network. The contract is vendor-neutral, so apps aren\'t tied to Scrib: they can bind any compatible transcriber the user has installed.</string>
